.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH wsblast-agent 1  "wsblast-agent 0.2.6" 
.SH NAME
wsblast\-agent \- Run a load agent that generates load for a coordinator (`wsblast URL \-\-agents ...`), one test at a time
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwsblast agent\fR [\fB\-\-token\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\-cert\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-source\-ip\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-listen\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a load agent that generates load for a coordinator (`wsblast URL \-\-agents ...`), one test at a time
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-listen\fR \fI<ADDR>\fR
Address to accept coordinators on (host:port, e.g. \*(Aq0.0.0.0:7700\*(Aq; port 0 picks a free port)
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<TOKEN>\fR
Token coordinators must present, at least 16 characters; required, here or in WSBLAST_AGENT_TOKEN
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-cert\fR \fI<PEM>\fR
PEM certificate chain to serve the control channel over TLS (wss://)
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-key\fR \fI<PEM>\fR
PEM private key for \-\-tls\-cert
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-ip\fR \fI<IP>\fR
Local addresses of this machine the tests\*(Aq connections bind in turn, comma\-separated or repeated, as \-\-source\-ip on one machine
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.2.6
